WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.041 --> 00:00:00.333
Okay wait,

00:00:00.333 --> 00:00:00.750
I just

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:01.501
learned something

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.961
that's kind of blowing my mind.

00:00:02.961 --> 00:00:03.294
The reason

00:00:03.294 --> 00:00:04.295
why there are so many

00:00:04.295 --> 00:00:06.297
Thai restaurants in the United States

00:00:06.297 --> 00:00:08.425
is because the government of Thailand

00:00:08.425 --> 00:00:09.634
wanted there to be.

00:00:09.634 --> 00:00:10.343
In 2002,

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:11.553
the government of Thailand, launched

00:00:11.553 --> 00:00:14.139
this program to train Thai chefs

00:00:14.139 --> 00:00:15.932
and then to invest in them

00:00:15.932 --> 00:00:17.517
opening restaurants in other countries.

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:19.227
And it was at this time in 2002

00:00:19.227 --> 00:00:20.812
that they chose pad thai

00:00:20.812 --> 00:00:22.188
to be their national dish.

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:23.273
And it totally worked.

00:00:23.273 --> 00:00:24.441
Now, there are thousands

00:00:24.441 --> 00:00:25.400
and thousands more

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:27.485
Thai restaurants here in our country

00:00:27.485 --> 00:00:28.319
and around the world

00:00:28.319 --> 00:00:29.779
because of this effort.

00:00:29.779 --> 00:00:30.405
Some people call it

00:00:30.405 --> 00:00:33.575
“gastrodiplomacy,” using food as a way

00:00:33.575 --> 00:00:36.161
to spread the goodness of your culture

00:00:36.161 --> 00:00:36.786
and your country

00:00:36.786 --> 00:00:37.871
to the rest of the world.

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:39.414
And I think it's freaking awesome.

00:00:39.414 --> 00:00:40.415
Thank you, Thailand.

00:00:40.415 --> 00:00:41.291
If you want to better understand

00:00:41.291 --> 00:00:43.251
global politics and stuff like this,

00:00:43.251 --> 00:00:44.419
follow along for more.

